 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Just One Cookbook’s recipe is curry udon; the broth is hers unchanged.</li><li>Putting it on soba (and the soba method, from her hot soba noodle soup) is this page’s swap.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Udon → soba"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>At soba shops, curry with leek or green onion on soba is “curry nanban”.</li><li>For more of the nanban leek, add <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> diagonally sliced Japanese leek (naganegi) with the onion — Sudachi’s curry udon does — untested here.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Curry nanban"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Sudachi makes the broth without roux: <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"500\" data-s=\"0\">500 ml</span> dashi, <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">3 tbsp</span> soy, <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tbsp</span> mirin, <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> sugar, thickened with <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">3 tbsp</span> Japanese curry powder mixed into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span> potato starch and <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 tbsp</span> cold water, simmered 10 minutes.</p>",
   "title_html": "No roux?"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>JOC: any protein instead of the pork — thin chicken thigh pieces work.</p>",
   "title_html": "Other protein"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>The broth keeps 3 days in the fridge and a month frozen; cook noodles fresh.</p>",
   "title_html": "Leftovers"
  }
 ],
